--- fig-U4-2.svg (19 text elements) ---
  A professional
  standard
  Guiding initial teacher training
  requires: enough detail to build a course on
  and a level a beginner can actually reach
  Guiding continuing development
  requires: room above the entry level, so an
  experienced teacher still has somewhere to go
  Informing appraisal
  requires: observable indicators, comparable
  between teachers, and a right of appeal
  A public accountability claim
  requires: language a parent or minister can
  read, and a promise the system can keep
  The four uses can conflict.
  Detail for training reads as
  bureaucracy in appraisal; language simple enough for the public is too coarse to develop anyone.
  A standard written for all four at once serves each of them a little worse.
  textbook.com.pk
