--- fig-U4-3.svg (19 text elements) ---
  Standard
  Knowledge and understanding
  what the teacher knows: subject content, how pupils learn it, where it is usually misunderstood
  Dispositions
  attitudes and values the teacher holds: that every pupil can learn, that errors are information
  Performance and skills
  what the teacher can do: the part that can be seen, and therefore the part that is assessed
  Indicator: plans for misconceptions
  Indicator: checks understanding mid-lesson
  Indicator: adapts when a check fails
  Evidence: a plan naming the
  wrong answer pupils give
  Evidence: observed question that
  was not answered by one pupil
  Evidence: the second explanation,
  different from the first
  Indicators sit beneath the parts, and only indicators produce evidence. The three shown below are drawn from performance
  and skills, the part that can be seen; what a teacher knows and values is inferred from what performance shows.
  textbook.com.pk
