  Admission
  to teacher education
  applied by: the institution
  at stake: entry
  Certification
  on completion
  applied by: the awarding body
  at stake: the qualification
  Licensing
  where required
  applied by: the state
  at stake: the right to teach
  Probation
  and confirmation
  applied by: the employer
  at stake: the post
  Periodic appraisal
  recurring
  applied by: the head
  at stake: standing, and pay
  Promotion
  or transfer
  applied by: the system
  at stake: the next role
  Re-licensing
  where it exists
  applied by: the state
  at stake: continuing to teach
  Dashed boxes are applied only where a jurisdiction requires them; the rest apply almost everywhere.
  One document is used seven times by six different parties, each wanting something different from it.
  That is why the same standard reads as guidance at admission and as a threat at appraisal. Nothing about the words changed; the stake did.
  textbook.com.pk
