  The two sets of requirements pull against each other
  Isore (2009) calls the purposes "often conflicting - but not necessarily incompatible": countries rarely use a pure form, one framework
  "can serve both", and an annex is devoted to conciliating them. A system serving both must decide in advance which purpose each
  conversation serves, who sees what, and what carries consequence.
  Left unstated, the summative purpose wins by default, because it is the one with a decision attached.
